new to Promethean. What kind of stopgap is needed other than just the player deciding that their character isn't made of dead bodies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T19:56:30-07:00","id":944669,"title":"","content":"If you're made of metal, it's harder to hurt you. If you're made of paper, you burn more easily. Just two examples. Also, it might affect how easy it is to make you in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T20:00:26-07:00","id":944670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>A Maker Dreaming:</b> Prometheans created through dreams. </div> </div> </div>This is actually touched on in the Extempore section and some of the fiction, although it's not expounded on quite as fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T21:43:15-07:00","id":944694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=944669#post944669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're made of metal, it's harder to hurt you. If you're made of paper, you burn more easily. Just two examples. Also comma it might affect how easy it is to make you in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T11:23:56-07:00","id":944960,"title":"","content":"For constructs, I'd recommend making a list of Bestowments that can model unusual materials, and maybe suggestions about milestones revolving around such an existence. Or, instead of Bestowments, use Merits, to keep Bestowments' additions to the lineages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T11:35:53-07:00","id":944970,"title":"","content":"A series of Construct Merits sounds like the best option, as Bestowments are supposed to highlight unique features of a specific Lineage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:49:43-07:00","id":945009,"title":"","content":"My only concern is that a Merit model turns it into an optimization choice, where Bestowments turn it into a conceptual choice, where I think it should be. As Bestowments, however, I'd still work constructs as Lineage-neutral. For me, I think Torment, Wasteland, and Disquiet effects do a good enough job distinguishing Lineages. But, alternatively, a construct trait could be worked like a kith, but zeroed out benefit-wise. A marble Muse might have have armor, but loses 10-again on Athletics; a sand sculpture Extempore might be able to pour through cracks, but reduces physical dice pools to a chance die while immersed in water.<br /> <br /> I think construct rules should say something essential about the character and hir creation, and I think that's better served outside a dot framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:30:02-07:00","id":945031,"title":"","content":"I was hoping about giving one Construct-related Bestowment if there would be two per character. But in <b>PtC</b> 2E character can have only one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then I remembered that in 1E <b>Strange Alchemies</b> Constructs <i>did</i> get their special powers as third kind Bestowments. Maybe go this way again, in 2E fan rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:53:05-07:00","id":945044,"title":"","content":"Player character Centimani are lacking some support, primarily the accrual of Alembics. No roles or milestones can be achieved. Therefore, each step back on the Refinement unlocks an Alembic, even if the Freak is on their last dot of Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T17:57:43-07:00","id":945774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945031#post945031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping about giving one Construct-related Bestowment if there would be two per character. But in <b>PtC</b> 2E character can have only one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then I remembered that in 1E <b>Strange Alchemies</b> Constructs <i>did</i> get their special powers as third kind Bestowments. Maybe go this way again, in 2E fan rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work: Construct Bestowments are a special type that you get in addition to your Lineage Bestowment, but only if you're a Construct. Most Unfleshed are Constructs; the few that aren't are Androids: assembled out of cloned or synthesized body parts rather than parts harvested from corpses. (Note: I'm intending to synthesize <b>Magnum Opus</b>' Constructs and <b>Saturnine Night</b>'s Unfleshed into a unified set of rules for Prometheans that are made out of materials other than flesh.)<br /> <br /> Every Construct Bestowment has a Drawback as well as a benefit. <br /> <br /> <u>Sample Construct Bestowments</u><br /> <b>Hard Body</b><br /> Your body is made of stone or metal. <br /> <i>Benefits:</i> You have Armor 2/2, and your unarmed attacks do Lethal damage as if you were armed. <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> Your basic Speed is 3, not 5. <br /> <br /> <b>Wooden Frame</b><br /> You're made of wood or some other lightweight and flammable material such as paper, plastic, or wax. <br /> <i>Benefit:</i> Bashing damage is halved.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> fire causes aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> To do: <br /> \u2022 The Generative Act<br /> \u2022 Pyros, Vitriol, and the Constructed Body<br /> <br /> The Generative Act: <br /> \u2022 Turning a statue into a Promethean should be a lot harder than turning a robot into a Promethean, because the Pyros has to do more work: a statue doesn't have articulated limbs, motors to move them, or a power supply to drive them; it doesn't have sensors to observe the environment or a digital brain to process the observations. And it doesn't have a circulatory system to distribute Azothic-charged fluid throughout the body. All of these are things that Pyros can compensate for; but the more it <i>needs</i> to compensate for, the harder the generative act is. <b>Magnum Opus</b> suggests a -4 penalty to the generative act if the body is made of anything but flesh; I'd suggest mitigating or eliminating this penalty the more machine-like the body is, for the reasons stated above. <br /> <br /> Pyros, Vitriol, and the Constructed Body:<br /> \u2022 Arguably, constructed Prometheans shouldn't have any natural healing ability: healing should require either a mechanic or an expenditure of Pyros. Likewise, <b>Magnum Opus</b> suggests that a construct needs to expend a point of Pyros every day to remain animate, canceling out the free point of Pyros that a Promethean generates every day; and it suggests that the construct's lack of a circulatory system means that it's easier to steal its Vitriol. It also mentions that hiding a construct's Disfigurements is beyond the Divine Flame's capacity, though <b>Saturnine Night</b>'s Unfleshed rules contradict this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-07-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:48:57-07:00","id":945985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945774#post945774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hard Body</b><br /> Your body is made of stone or metal.<br /> <i>Benefits:</i> You have Armor 2/2, and your unarmed attacks do Lethal damage as if you were armed.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> Your basic Speed is 3, not 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good for me<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945774#post945774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wooden Frame</b><br /> You're made of wood or some other lightweight and flammable material such as paper, plastic, or wax.<br /> <i>Benefit:</i> Bashing damage is halved.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> fire causes aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>ALL Created take Aggravated damage from fire - see Drawbacks on page 171. Maybe Wooden Created will take <i>double</i> Aggravated damage from fire?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945774#post945774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Generative Act:<br /> \u2022 Turning a statue into a Promethean should be a lot harder than turning a robot into a Promethean, because the Pyros has to do more work: a statue doesn't have articulated limbs, motors to move them, or a power supply to drive them; it doesn't have sensors to observe the environment or a digital brain to process the observations. And it doesn't have a circulatory system to distribute Azothic-charged fluid throughout the body. All of these are things that Pyros can compensate for; but the more it <i>needs</i> to compensate for, the harder the generative act is. <b>Magnum Opus</b> suggests a -4 penalty to the generative act if the body is made of anything but flesh; I'd suggest mitigating or eliminating this penalty the more machine-like the body is, for the reasons stated above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems resonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945774#post945774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pyros, Vitriol, and the Constructed Body:<br /> \u2022 Arguably, constructed Prometheans shouldn't have any natural healing ability: healing should require either a mechanic or an expenditure of Pyros. Likewise, <b>Magnum Opus</b> suggests that a construct needs to expend a point of Pyros every day to remain animate, canceling out the free point of Pyros that a Promethean generates every day; and it suggests that the construct's lack of a circulatory system means that it's easier to steal its Vitriol. It also mentions that hiding a construct's Disfigurements is beyond the Divine Flame's capacity, though <b>Saturnine Night</b>'s Unfleshed rules contradict this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with Unfleshed rules interpretation - <b>Magnum Opus </b>one sounds too harsh and you poined that want to treat Constructs as quasi-Unfleshed in first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:04:29-07:00","id":946438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=945985#post945985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ALL Created take Aggravated damage from fire - see Drawbacks on page 171. Maybe Wooden Created will take <i>double</i> Aggravated damage from fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah there, double is not a good idea, in that it is terrifying. +2 or +3 at most, which is still pretty harsh. Arguably, wax would increase the severity of an Extreme Environment (Heat) up by one; paper, while probably coated in shellac, would be both flammable and incompatible with water. Wood, in this instance, wouldn't really be living wood (as in a living tree, which do not burn easy) or dead wood (as in what you put in a fireplace to actually make a fire) but in the weird Promethean in-between, and that brings up issues of whether or not you have to replace damage or grow it back.<br /> <br /> I can picture a wooden Promethean cursed with having to maintain herself like a bonsai garden. Somebody hit her with a hatchet in the shoulder; now she has to lug around a watering can. Water twice daily, plenty of sunlight.<br /> <br /> In the instance of simple draw-backs I'd say &quot;pick an environment or element inhospitable to your character's construction; treat all Extreme Environment Tilts as one worse for them, and any major concentration of that element can cause complications up to and including Aggravated Damage.&quot; The later clause can be fairly tricky to balance, though, but it would allow a wooden Promethean to say that axes, saws, and the like inflict Agg on them. <br /> <br /> (by element, here, I of course mean &quot;element of nature,&quot; not &quot;I cast Ice Storm&quot;).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:43:34-07:00","id":948076,"title":"","content":"Athanors, 1e-style, are a Z-Splat that provides a pair of Traits that can be improved using Vitriol; a pool of Reagent that can be spent to mitigate various difficulties Prometheans encounter; and a Boon that provides a small Lineage-based power that can be traded in for a thematically appropriate non-supernatural benefit when the New Dawn is achieved. For 2e purposes, I'm reassigning each of these to some other aspect of the character: the Affinity Traits become part of the Roles; the Reagent pool becomes a type of (2e-style) Athanor that acts as an augmented version of the Vitriol Fount; and the Boons become an extension of a reimagined Bestowment system. In order:<br /> <br /> <u>Role Traits</u><br /> Each Role has two traits associated with it. While you're in that role, you may spend Vitriol Experiences to improve those Traits. <br /> <br /> I have not yet looked at he Roles with this in mind; any suggestions as to which Traits should be associated with which Roles are welcome. <br /> <br /> <u>Vitriol Fount</u><br /> Like the Vitriol Founts presented in 2e, you can extract Vitriol from this version of the Vitriol Fount. However, you choose exactly how much is in there (by spending one Vitriol for each dot that's in there); it doesn't regenerate (if you want more in there, invest more Vitriol); and it generates a new \u201cfuel stat\u201d called Reagent that behaves according to the Reagent rules found in 1e's Athanors chapter. <br /> <br /> <u>Boons</u><br /> Boons are now joined with Bestowments, in that Bestowments are now a type of Boons. You get the option to purchase a Boon at Azoth 1, 3, 5, 7, and 9; at Azoth 1, the Boon must be a Lineage-appropriate Bestowment; but you get it automatically. Later \u201cBoon slots\u201d cost one Vitriol Experience each to fill if the Boon is Lineage-appropriate; two otherwise. When you achieve the New Dawn, you may Redeem your Boons for thematically related non-supernatural benefits (see 1e's Redeemed Boons for examples). Reagent costs for Boons are recast as Pyros costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:47:52-07:00","id":948138,"title":"","content":"Automatons are \u201cAzoth 0 Prometheans\u201d. They serve as an expansion 1e's Clones, and are defined by their lack of free will (for which you'll find guidelines in P1e under \u201cClones\u201d). Automatons have Lineages and Bestowments/Boons, but they have Integrity instead of Pilgrimage, and they lack Refinements, Roles, and Transmutations. 1e-style Clones are Androids (flesh-made Unfleshed) with at least a dot in Famous Face. <br /> <br /> Automatons can be thought of as half-completed Prometheans: the body is already prepared, all that's needed is immersion in the appropriate element and investment of a dot of Azoth. Do that, and the Automaton is upgraded to a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:07:00-07:00","id":948157,"title":"","content":"I havne't gotten to the part about alchemists yet, but question - is it possible that clones are included in the alchemist section? I mean, the original clones in 1e were nothing more than a slave to someone who was hunting down Prometheans for their experiments in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:18:43-07:00","id":948162,"title":"","content":"Would Reagent be full Vitriol Experiences or just Vitriol Beats? Seems a little weighty to have them be full Experiences, especially since Pandorans can burn Beats as Pyros.<br /> <br /> Maybe Reagent could be used to make the effects of a Distillation in the Refinement's Transmutations permanent, with Storyteller discretion?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Automatons but perhaps, instead of Automatons, they could be called Homunculi. Perhaps there could be a Firestorm Aspect, as in 1e, that raises corpses as proto-Prometheans, or in this case Automatons/Homunculi.<br /> <br /> If I could suggest an alternative name for the Boons? Since they're tied to Lineage, why not call them Heirlooms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:50:20-07:00","id":948245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948162#post948162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Reagent be full Vitriol Experiences or just Vitriol Beats? Seems a little weighty to have them be full Experiences, especially since Pandorans can burn Beats as Pyros.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would indeed be Beats:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Once a point of Vitriol is placed into the Athanor, it creates a pool of temporary points (similar to a character's pool of Willpower points) that can be spent for various effects. These points are called Reagents, because they effect change. Each Vitriol point that is \u201cbanked\u201d into the Athanor increases the Reagent pool by one point. (It might be helpful to view Vitriol points that are deposited into the Athanor as dots, which allow for Reagent points.)</span></div>\u2014 PtC1e, p.261<br /> <br /> For clarity's sake: Reagent can never be spent faster than a point per turn, and it recovers at a rate of a point per day. (Although I'm debating saying that you can spend an additional number of Reagent per turn equal to the number of Vitriol <i>Experiences</i> that you've banked in the Vitriol Fount.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948162#post948162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Reagent could be used to make the effects of a Distillation in the Refinement's Transmutations permanent, with Storyteller discretion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm\u2026 no. It's already been established that <i>access to</i> an Alembic costs two Vitriol Experiences; making a Distillations effect permanent should be harder to pull off, not easier. Reagent regenerates on its own, unlike Vitriol. Its existing uses are to temporarily boost your supernatural resistance by one, to reduce a Disquiet check against you by one die, to enhance your resistance against a Torment check by one die, to hide your Disfigurements for a turn, or to halve your Azothic Radiance for a scene. Its effects are supposed to be temporary. Heck, even the two uses that require spending a Reagent <i>dot</i> (i.e., a Vitriol Beat) \u2014 forcing a Pandoran into Dormancy and forcing a Promethean out of Torment \u2014 aren't what I'd call permanent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948162#post948162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Automatons but perhaps, instead of Automatons, they could be called Homunculi. Perhaps there could be a Firestorm Aspect, as in 1e, that raises corpses as proto-Prometheans, or in this case Automatons/Homunculi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. \u201cAutomaton\u201d works for a Constructed Homunculus, and Firestorm-generated Homunculi should be temporary and Extempore \u2014 that is, they don't last beyond the Firestorm, and aren'tsuitable candidates for Generative Act completion. Usually. Exceptions are left to Storyteller discretion, and generally become Extempore Prometheans <i>during</i> the Firestorm without any intervention by others. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948162#post948162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could suggest an alternative name for the Boons? Since they're tied to Lineage, why not call them Heirlooms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like Boons; but I'm willing to be persuaded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:53:22-07:00","id":948248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=944463#post944463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absence of Going to the Wastes surprised me</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to separate it from just being Cuprum hermit though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:01:14-07:00","id":948254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948248#post948248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard to separate it from just being Cuprum hermit though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not hard at all. Going to the Wastes is like turning a robot's power supply off: for the duration, you stand around completely insensate while your Azoth slowly discharges. A Cuprum hermit isolates itself from humanity; but it remains active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:26:00-07:00","id":948508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948254#post948254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not hard at all. Going to the Wastes is like turning a robot's power supply off: for the duration, you stand around completely insensate while your Azoth slowly discharges. A Cuprum hermit isolates itself from humanity; but it remains active.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't recall a hibernation state being described at all, I just remember the book talking about going into seclusion away from any contact with others. I'll have to go back and check 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:45:30-07:00","id":948632,"title":"","content":"It's not <i>quite</i> that severe in 1e:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">The method differs by Promethean as well. Some hibernate. Some shut down certain bodily systems. Others stand, immobile, in forest glades or on blasted plains, effectively becoming features of the landscape themselves. Still others remain active in their isolated environments, simply eschewing interpersonal contact.</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Promethean: the Created</b> first edition, p.208</div>I <i>do</i> think that in 2e, there should be some sort of \u201cLethargy penalty\u201d if a Promethean who is Going to the Wastes chooses to remain active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:53:02-07:00","id":948634,"title":"","content":"The pandoran Mockeries, their equivalents of lineages, appear to be gone as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:39:20-07:00","id":948679,"title":"","content":"The Scion rules are fine as far as they go; the only problem is that they don't go far enough, completely neglecting the mechanics of pregnancy. Fortunately, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/pregnancy-in-the-world-of-darkness/\" target=\"_blank\">there's a blog for that</a>. The main thing I'd change would be to say that each stage of pregnancy counts as a major milestone for the Promethean parent (although Promethean fathers need to stay engaged in the process to reach the milestones), and successful childbirth can count as the Multiplicatio universal milestone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T13:33:37-07:00","id":948811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=948634#post948634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pandoran Mockeries, their equivalents of lineages, appear to be gone as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think they're coming back, I think they're leaning into Pandorans being more diversely freeform instead of all fitting into these specific categories that guarantee some of the same powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:12:28-07:00","id":949010,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the point of the thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:05:54-07:00","id":949118,"title":"","content":"If Dataweaver doesn't do a write-up for the Mockeries, I'm going to. They were limiting but I liked the flavor, and I think they'd be fine as another layer of terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:21:26-07:00","id":952822,"title":"","content":"The Prodigal Demiurge doesn't have much in the way of mechanics; what it <i>does</i> have (the correlation of Lineages with Vices) is outmoded with ChroD's new system for Virtue and Vice. Port a trimmed-down version of it into 2e as yet another theory about the Principle's nature, possibly with the added notion that every time a Promethean Redeems, the Prodigal Demiurge gets one step closer to returning to Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:27:55-07:00","id":952829,"title":"","content":"<b>Going to the Wastes</b><br /> The Promethean cuts himself off from all contact and effectively shuts down in order to give himself a chance to \u201ccool off\u201d. The process is a lot like a Pandoran going Dormant, except that it's entirely voluntary on the Promethean's part: he can enter or exit this state of consciousness at will. <br /> <br /> The effects of Going to the Waste are to lower your Azoth, earn a Condition that helps you resist Torment, and generate and Fester a Wasteland. It takes one season (three months) for every dot that you reduce your Azoth; and each season earns or strengthens the Cool Head Condition (see below). <br /> <br /> Time spent going to the wastes doesn't count toward the Promethean's age; in fact, the discharge of Azoth can extend the Promethean's lifespan: <i>subtract</i> time spent going to the waste from the Promethean's effective age. <br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Cool Head</b><br /> Your character has gone to the wastes recently, cooling down his Azoth. As such, she has earned a bonus to resist Torment. Each dot of Azoth shed by going to the Wastes translates to a bonus die to resist Torment for as long as you have this Condition. <br /> <i>Resolution:</i> this benefit dissipates by one die per season, or the next time the Promethean raises his Azoth. <br /> <br /> You cannot go to the wastes while you have the Cool Head Condition; this replaces the original rules' requirement to wait a year or longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-17-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:36:45-07:00","id":952833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944450-left-behind?p=952829#post952829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to the Wastes doesn't require any mechanical updates either, beyond saying that Going to the Wastes involves enough Pyros expenditure to set up a Wasteland marker. That is, Going to the Wastes doesn't necessarily involve going to a wasteland (capitalized or lower case); but by the time you're done, you <i>will be</i> in a Wasteland. So it's a good idea to find an out-of-the-way place to do it, where you won't disturb anyone nor be disturbed.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I'm moderately certain that Jovian Athanors serve some of the old purpose of Going to the Wastes, between shedding Persistent Conditions and potentially lowering your Azoth or Festering a Wasteland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:20:40-07:00","id":952867,"title":"","content":"It's certainly similar. Still, the differences are important:<br /> \u2022 you don't need to have mastered a Refinement to Go to the Wastes; you can do it at any time. <br /> \u2022 creating a Jovian Athanor doesn't lower your Azoth or provide bonus dice to resist Torment. Incidentally, those bonus dice ought to be phrased as a Condition that you can acquire by going to the wastes.<br /> \u2022 Going to the Wastes takes time. Months of time. In 1e, it was one month to discharge the first dot of Azoth, two months to discharge the second, and so on. <br /> <br /> (Note: I didn't refamiliarize myself sufficiently with 1e's Going to the Wastes mechanics before posting; for that, I apologize. I've revised the post accordingly.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-17-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}